footer  (fixed, the gates as they stand, the findings as they stand {'UPDATE_INSERTS_A_GEAR_ON_2024': None, 'UPDATE_BANDS_IN_PLACE_ON_2024': None}) [red] Update SolidWorks would add Hub on Output (a new part, Hub_m1.25_N17), as its shaft's anchor with RangeSlv splined to it, give RangeSlv its bands in Sleeve_m1.25_N17, change RangeSlv's values (Sleeve_m1.25_N17), and move RangeSlv in H to 55.5 mm and in N to 48 mm and in L to 40.5 mm along Output. It was built with a configuration per mode (H, N and L), each named as its mode, and saved in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. A turn you give the gears in one mode can show in other modes, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. Carrier (the carrier) is axes and planes only, so it has nothing to drag. The next press would stop before changing anything: Update SolidWorks would insert a gear into the assembly and mate it and give a built sleeve its bands in its own part, which Gear Generator has not yet been shown to do on SolidWorks 2024 (findings.UPDATE_INSERTS_A_GEAR_ON_2024 and findings.UPDATE_BANDS_IN_PLACE_ON_2024), so the press changes nothing; Build again… makes the new revision instead.
